REMARKS:
240300Z POSITION NEAR 18.4N 83.6E.
24SEP26. TROPICAL CYCLONE 01B (ONE), LOCATED APPROXIMATELY 378 NM
SOUTHWEST OF KOLKATA, INDIA, HAS TRACKED NORTHWESTWARD AT 01
KNOTS OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS. RADAR IMAGERY CONFIRMS THAT THE
LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER HAS MADE LANDFALL BETWEEN SRIKAKULUM
AND VIZIANAGARUM. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED IMAGERY DEPICTS THE
DEEP CONVECTION THAT HAD BEEN PERSISTENT IS NOW SHRINKING,
INDICATING THAT THEE SYSTEM IS ON A WEAKENING TREND. THE LLCC
WILL CONTINUE TO TRACK INLAND ON A NORTH-NORTHWESTWARD TRAJECTORY,
WITH DISSIPATION PREDICTED BY TAU 24. THIS IS THE FINAL WARNING ON
THIS SYSTEM BY THE JOINT TYPHOON WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI. THE SYSTEM
WILL BE CLOSELY MONITORED FOR SIGNS OF REGENERATION. MINIMUM CENTRAL
PRESSURE AT 240000Z IS 987 MB.
